  required_positive:
  - Ordered outer tiers compile to deterministic descending internal priority values (`N..1`), because current V3 Target selects the maximum numeric priority.
  - Omitted weights in one multi-member tier compile to equal weights.
  - Different TOML table ordering and explicit equal weights produce the same normalized authoring and Manifest output.
  - The projected authoring enters the existing Config03, Config04, and Config05 functions without a second compiler.
  - Exact basename config.toml selects V3UserConfigStore once in the Config owner and server status consumes its loaded snapshot.
